SUMMARY:Disposable Humanity Screening and Q&A
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Ware Center for a free screening of the film Disposable Humanity—plus a community discussion panel and a Q&A with the filmmakers.  \n\n\n\n The Mitchell family—esteemed Disability Studies scholars and filmmakers—delve into the chilling legacy of the Nazi Aktion T4 program. This investigative documentary recounts the long-obscured history of how over 300\,000 disabled individuals became the initial victims of the Third Reich. Targeted by the T4 program as having a “life unworthy of living\,” their murders laid the groundwork for the Holocaust that followed. 6:15 PM • Pre-show community panel discussion Post-show • Q&A with director Cameron S. Mitchell Co-presented by the MU Disability Film Festival and Congregation Shaarai Shomayim. \n\n\n\n\n    Buy Tickets
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/disposable-humanity-screening-and-qa/
LOCATION:Ware Center for the Arts\, 42 N. Prince St.\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17603\, United States
CATEGORIES:Arts & Entertainment
ORGANIZER;CN="Millersville University Office of Visual & Performing Arts":MAILTO:cori.jackson@millersville.edu
END:VEVENT
