SUMMARY:"Education Impact: Right for ALL" Community Breakfast
DESCRIPTION:The Lancaster Education Foundation will bring together business\, civic\, and education leaders for its annual signature breakfast event\, Education Impact: Right for ALL\, a community conversation focused on the future of public education and opportunities for students throughout Lancaster. \n\n\n\n The breakfast will feature a panel of prominent local leaders\, including: Dr. Keith Miles\, Superintendent of the School District of LancasterThe Honorable Jaime Arroyo\, Mayor of the City of Lancaster Heather Valudes\, CEO of the Lancaster Chamber of Commerce.  \n\n\n\nTogether\, they will share perspectives on education\, workforce development\, community collaboration\, and the importance of creating opportunities that support all students. The event aligns with the week of The ExtraGive\, a strategic time when community organizations and local residents unite to support causes that strengthen Lancaster County. By hosting breakfast during this high-visibility week\, the Foundation aims to highlight our shared responsibility to ensure equitable educational opportunities for every student. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n    Buy Tickets
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/education-impact-right-for-all-community-breakfast/
LOCATION:Lancaster-Lebanon IU-13\, 1020 New Holland Ave\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Community
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/10/Breakfast-Ad.avif
END:VEVENT
