SUMMARY:PDF@Zoetropolis Presents Minari
DESCRIPTION:Our November America 250 selection\, Lee Isaac Chung’s Minari\, follows a Korean American family pursuing a new life on a small Arkansas farm in the early 1980s.\n\nIt is a deeply American story of immigration\, land\, work\, faith\, family\, and reinvention—but also a searching examination of the costs hidden within the American dream. Who bears the burden of one person’s ambition? Does independence ever exist without care and dependency? What transforms a piece of land into a home?\n\nArriving during harvest and Thanksgiving season\, Minari also asks us to think about cultivation and gratitude: whose labor sustains a family\, whose histories inhabit the land\, and what conditions allow transplanted lives to flourish. Its answer is both modest and profound: nothing grows entirely on its own. \n            \n        \n                \n            \n                \n                \n    Learn More
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/pdfzoetropolis-presents-minari/
LOCATION:Zoetropolis Cinema Stillhouse\, 112 North Water Street\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17603\, United States
CATEGORIES:Arts & Entertainment
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/11/minari-landscape-pic.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="Zoetropolis Cinema Stillhouse":MAILTO:info@zoetropolis.com
END:VEVENT
